# Capability Capsule protocols

A **Capability Capsule (CC)** is a versioned, installable package that exposes one or more related operations. The declaration tells a caller what it can ask the tool to do. The immutable release identifies the implementation that answers. A receipt records what happened on one call.

```text
Author → YAML declaration → Software Factory → immutable CC release
                                 │                    │
                                 ▼                    ▼
                            build record       qualified catalog
                                 ▲                    │ discover operation
                                 │                    ▼
                                 │                Lab agent
                                 │                    │ request + inputs
                                 │                    ▼
                                 └── release pin ── bound call → runner
                                                      ▲            │
                                                      │            ├── outputs
                                                      └── receipt ─┘      │
                                                             │            │
                                                             └─────┬──────┘
                                                                   ▼
                                                         independent evaluation
```

A Factory brief can also produce a candidate engine image with zero CCs. In the Muse workflow, the candidate engine is the **subject** being measured. The profiler or benchmark CC is the **instrument**. The Lab binds the two at call time and records both identities.

## The small case

```yaml
cc: "1"
id: text.trim
version: 1.0.0
carrier: fixture.invalid/text@sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
does: Remove leading and trailing ASCII spaces. An all-space input returns an empty string.
run: /tools/trim
takes: {text: string}
gives: {trimmed: string}
```

**Caller view · `text.trim/run`.** Supply one string named `text`. Read the returned string from `trimmed`, including when it is empty. No provider or external mutation is declared. The runner checks the output type. A number fails input validation before launch. A process crash yields a failed receipt. The image pin above is a design fixture.

